meta {
  name: stacks: member pod
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "pod_id": "myn8nmain",
    "stack_id": "{{stack_id}}",
    "image": "n8nio/n8n:latest",
    "depends_on": ["myn8ndb", "myn8nredis"],
    "ready_condition": "available",
    "networking": {
      "default": { "protocol": "http", "port": 5678 }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  ## Joining a stack at create time (runtime, no template)
  - `stack_id` — join an existing stack you have USER+ on. The pod inherits stack permissions.
  - `depends_on` — **same-stack pod_ids** the runner waits on before starting this pod.
  - `ready_condition` — `available` (container running) or `ready` (readiness probe passing;
    requires `healthchecks.readiness`).

  Note: cross-pod **secrets and hosts** here must be wired by hand (a Tapis SK secret referenced
  in each pod, and the dependency's pod_id as the host). The **stack template** flow automates
  exactly this — see `Create stack template tag (n8n)`.
}
